RELATED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS (quick answers)
================================================================================

Q: REST vs SOAP?
A: REST is lightweight JSON over HTTP; SOAP is XML + WSDL, heavier, common in banks.

Q: REST vs GraphQL?
A: REST has many endpoints / fixed response shape; GraphQL has one endpoint and client picks fields.

Q: When Kafka instead of REST between services?
A: When you need async, high throughput, and loose coupling (fire event, don’t wait).

Q: What does API Gateway do?
A: Single entry: auth, rate limit, routing, logging — clients don’t call microservices directly.

Q: Is CRUD same as REST?
A: CRUD is the create/read/update/delete style usually implemented WITH REST; REST can do more than CRUD.


================================================================================
Interview Tip (Important ⭐)
================================================================================

If interviewer asks:

Which API pattern do you prefer and why?

Answer:

“I mostly use RESTful APIs with proper HTTP methods, pagination, versioning, and API Gateway for microservices.
For async communication between services, I prefer event-driven APIs using Kafka.
For action-style internal calls I may use RPC/gRPC, and for complex UI data needs GraphQL can help.”


One-Line Summary
REST = resources + HTTP verbs | RPC = call a function remotely | GraphQL = ask for exact fields
Events = async via bus | Webhook = server calls you | Gateway = one door | BFF = backend per UI
